{
  "day": 18,
  "title": "Present perfect",
  "units": [
    {
      "id": 28,
      "code": "G",
      "title": "Present perfect",
      "rule": "Present perfect *have/has + feʼlning 3-shakli* bilan yasaladi. U natijani yoki hayotdagi tajribani bildiradi, aniq vaqt aytilmaydi: *I have visited Samarkand.* — Men Samarqandga borganman. *He, she, it* bilan *has*, qolganlari bilan *have*: *She has finished.* Toʻgʻri feʼllarga *-ed* qoʻshamiz (*visited, washed*), notoʻgʻri feʼllarning 3-shaklini yodlaymiz: *go – gone, see – seen, eat – eaten, buy – bought, write – written*. Savolda *Have you ever…?* (qachondir); *never* (hech qachon), *just* (hozirgina), *already* (allaqachon) feʼl oldiga qoʻyiladi; *yet* (hali) inkor va savolda gap oxiriga keladi: *I haven't eaten yet.*",
      "examples": [
        "I have visited Samarkand.",
        "Dilnoza has just finished her lesson.",
        "Bekzod has already eaten his lunch.",
        "I have never written a letter.",
        "Have you ever met Mr Kim?",
        "Aziz hasn't finished his homework yet."
      ],
      "words": [
        { "en": "ever", "uz": "qachondir (savolda)" },
